    },
    {
      "id": "content-starts-at-header-bottom",
      "metric": "mainGap",
      "when": "all",
      "target": 0,
      "tol": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "no-horizontal-overflow",
      "metric": "overflowX",
      "when": "all",
      "target": 0,
      "tol": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "content-left-edge",
      "metric": "contentLeft",
      "when": "full",
      "pair": 1,
      "feature": "f3"
    },
    {
      "id": "h1-aligned-with-lockup",
      "metric": "contentLeft",
      "sameAsMetric": "brandLeft",
      "tol": 1,
      "when": "full",
      "feature": "f3"
    }
  ],
  "breakpoints": {
    "full": 1440,
    "row": 780,
    "provenance": "row: MEASURED. Chromium (playwright) laid out the repo's own Manrope and Karla woff2 files: SAOC CTA 'Join a society' 120.4 + 48 = 168.4, NOS 'Tickets' 61.3 + 48 = 109.3 (matches the live 109), MENU button 104. Row = 405 lockup + 24 + 168.4 + 24 + 104 = 725.4 content; content = W - 2*clamp(16px,2.5vw,32px) gives W >= 764; 780 adds a 16px margin for a classic scrollbar. full: PROVISIONAL, see below. SAOC nav at 600 14.5px/1 Manrope = items 497.7 + 7*18 padding + 6*2 gaps = 635.7; bar = 405 + 24 + 635.7 + 24 + 44 + 24 + 168.4 = 1325.1px, but the content box never exceeds 1320px (--nc-wide), so the full row cannot fit at the spec's numbers at ANY width (5.1px short). 1440 is NOS Design's start value; the gate will fail at it until the spec changes. Not confirmed by a build yet: the gate measures the real header at full-1, full, row-1 and row.",
